# Grain — what one row means

## Declare it first, in business terms

- Not "one row per day" — **"one row per product per order"**
- The **most important** decision; everything else follows

## The grain fixes the rest

- **Dimensions** — anything true at that detail can attach
- **Measures** — only numbers true *at that grain* belong

## Prefer the finest grain

- Atomic rows **roll up** to any summary
- You can never **roll down** — lost detail is gone forever

## The cardinal sin

- **Never mix grain** — every row means the *same* thing
- A different level = a **separate** fact table
